SUMMARY
Jus de Chaussette, a trendy French sock company, has received an extortion email. As an intern at a cybersecurity firm, you work alongside your mentor Mio to investigate whether the attackers really stole sensitive data.

Your investigation traces the full attack chain: from a malicious file uploaded through the company's contact form, through credential dumping and customer database theft, to internal phishing targeting the CEO and CFO, and finally exfiltration of confidential files.

LEARNING OBJECTIVES
- Investigate an extortion incident from initial alert to full attack reconstruction
- Trace data staging and exfiltration using legitimate Windows tools (bitsadmin, Winrar)
- Identify credential dumping tools (LaZagne) and their targets
- Recognize command and control channels (dnscat2 over DNS)
- Follow internal phishing from compromised employee accounts
- Pivot across tables using KQL lookup and let statements
- Trace initial access through web application abuse (file upload forms)
- Connect attacker infrastructure using PassiveDNS pivoting

SOURCE
https://kc7cyber.com/challenges/355

